Competitive Landscape
The dominance of original OEMs-Boeing and Airbus-continues to shape the ecosystem. Integration of connectivity modules into new generation airframes, coupled with extensive maintenance networks, gives OEMs leverage to bundle connectivity as a standard offering. Honeywell aerospace, Thales Group, Garmin, and Collins Aerospace supply aircraft level hardware; L3Harris, Viasat, and Gogo provide satellite and in flight Wi Fi solutions; Siemens and Safran focus on data analytics layers. This diversity demands strict certification alignment and secure end to end delivery.
